<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Như Nguyệt River</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1077</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dai-viet-war">Song–Đại Việt war</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Như Nguyệt River was fought in 1077 on the Cầu river, then called Như Nguyệt, north of the Vietnamese capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thăng Long</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ly-thuong-kiet">Lý Thường Kiệt</a>'s fortified line held back a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> Chinese army under Guo Kui, sent in response to Đại Việt's raid of 1075–1076. Weakened by disease and failed crossings, the Song withdrew and peace was agreed, preserving Đại Việt's independence.</p></div>
